1:1 COMMENT "# typed_data.z -- data blocks whose `out` names their value type."
1:66 EOL "\n"
2:1 COMMENT "#"
2:2 EOL "\n"
3:1 COMMENT "# A data block has ONE element type, settled where it is written:"
3:66 EOL "\n"
4:1 COMMENT "#   - `data { ... } out intdata u8`  the value type's argument names it"
4:72 EOL "\n"
5:1 COMMENT "#   - `data { 1.u8 2 3 }`            the elements' own tags name it, and must agree"
5:84 EOL "\n"
6:1 COMMENT "#   - `data { ... }`                 neither: the elements are untyped, read as"
6:80 EOL "\n"
7:1 COMMENT "#                                    literals, and the block's value holds them as"
7:83 EOL "\n"
8:1 COMMENT "#                                    i64s, or f64s when every one is a float"
8:77 EOL "\n"
9:1 COMMENT "#"
9:2 EOL "\n"
10:1 COMMENT "# A value the chosen type cannot hold is an error at the declaration, not a"
10:76 EOL "\n"
11:1 COMMENT "# truncation at each read."
11:27 EOL "\n"
12:1 COMMENT "#"
12:2 EOL "\n"
13:1 COMMENT "# When the block is a constant lookup table of bytes / small ints,"
13:67 EOL "\n"
14:1 COMMENT "# `out intdata u8` keeps the C-level array narrow (one byte per slot"
14:69 EOL "\n"
15:1 COMMENT "# instead of eight) without forcing per-element `.u8` suffixes."
15:64 EOL "\n"
16:1 EOL "\n"
17:1 COMMENT "# Typed: every element pinned to u8. The C emitter lays this out"
17:65 EOL "\n"
18:1 COMMENT "# as `static const uint8_t[]`."
18:31 EOL "\n"
19:1 LABEL "bytemask"
19:9 COLON ":"
19:10 WS " "
19:11 DATA "data"
19:15 WS " "
19:16 BRACEOPEN "{"
19:17 EOL "\n"
20:1 WS "    "
20:5 LABEL "LOW"
20:8 COLON ":"
20:9 WS " "
20:10 REFID "0"
20:11 EOL "\n"
21:1 WS "    "
21:5 LABEL "MID"
21:8 COLON ":"
21:9 WS " "
21:10 REFID "64"
21:12 EOL "\n"
22:1 WS "    "
22:5 LABEL "HIGH"
22:9 COLON ":"
22:10 WS " "
22:11 REFID "250"
22:14 EOL "\n"
23:1 BRACECLOSE "}"
23:2 WS " "
23:3 OUT "out"
23:6 WS " "
23:7 REFID "intdata"
23:14 WS " "
23:15 REFID "u8"
23:17 EOL "\n"
24:1 EOL "\n"
25:1 COMMENT "# No clause and no tags: the elements are untyped, and as a value the block"
25:76 EOL "\n"
26:1 COMMENT "# is an `intdata i64`."
26:23 EOL "\n"
27:1 EOL "\n"
28:1 LABEL "primes"
28:7 COLON ":"
28:8 WS " "
28:9 DATA "data"
28:13 WS " "
28:14 BRACEOPEN "{"
28:15 WS " "
28:16 REFID "2"
